A||||9||JMStargazer||Gotta question 'bout my Fiero||||5||
Z||000000||JMStargazer||12-23-2000||09:18 PM||||Okay folks...let's see if someone's expertise can help me out.  I have an '86 2M4 that was vandalized (all the glass is gone) and it has been sitting in a garage for the past 5 years (it belonged to my boyfriend).  What potential problems could there be from it sitting so long?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||12-23-2000||10:19 PM||||Battery might go dead from sitting so long.<P>Does the engine turn over?  If it doesn't, that would be the first thing I'd check.<P>BTW, Welcome to the Forum!||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||12-23-2000||10:21 PM||||Prob not too much believe it or not. Id start off by replacing all the fluids, including the gas. Check and make sure no dry rot on belts or hoses, and it prob wouldnt hurt to replace those to..not to mention the obvious, the battery!<BR>Ive heard of people starting their Fieros up after 7,8, even 9 years with little problems (provided it was in good working order when it began its "hibernation"...<BR>Welcome to the forum!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||JMStargazer||12-23-2000||10:35 PM||||wow...I'm impressed.  you guys are quick.  I don't think there's too much wrong with it that a good tune-up won't fix.  The steering wheel doesn't lock, and the parking brake fails to engage occasionally, but that's about it.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000004||Tina||12-23-2000||10:51 PM||||Please make sure to post some pic,s<BR>when you're all done cleaning it up.<BR>We need  more documented sightings of <BR>Fiero's owned by women.<P>Welcome to the Forum<P>Tina||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||12-23-2000||11:08 PM||||If it was vandalized consider pulling the fuel tank before doing anything. not just siphoning it out. God know what might be down there. Pump junk up to the motor and you can ruin it. <P>While the tank is out fill it with water and check for leaks. (Take out the fuel pump.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||JMStargazer||12-23-2000||11:51 PM||||Nothing else was damaged 'cept for the windows.  Just some rowdy little hooligans that targeted the car because it was parked too long in one area.  (GRRRRRRRRRRR)<p>[This message has been edited by JMStargazer (edited 12-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||AL||12-24-2000||03:15 AM||||welcome aboard.if you have a sunroof don't stargaze while driving lol<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000008||KRMFiero||12-24-2000||08:44 AM||||besides from battery, hoses, GAS,     make sure you pull the spark plugs out and put some type of non-flammable penitrateing oil down there (Mistery oil is the best, liquid wrench works...) it is very harmful to your engine if you do not<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
